From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:31:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] fix(kanban): a local request-allowance stop is a
 neutral deferral on the native rate-limit path

RHOAI3 v15 (V15-1 change 1, tmp/v15-run-20260925/V15-1-DURABLE-QUOTA-
DESIGN.md section 2). A worker that stops on the run's local request
allowance (the next eligible slot is beyond the 900 s per-attempt wait) was
recorded through the failed-worker recorder: immediate respawn, the same
stop 3 s later, gave_up, blocked card. A predictable local wait is neither a
failure nor a reason for an immediate retry.

- request_pacer: RequestBudgetExhausted carries a structured deferral
  (accounting mode, retry_not_before = when the needed capacity becomes
  eligible, allowance); consumers never parse the STOP message.
- Worker: persists one local_budget_deferral event bound to its task and
  worker run (with model and accounting mode) BEFORE exiting, then leaves
  through the pinned native temporary-rate-limit exit,
  KANBAN_RATE_LIMIT_EXIT_CODE (cli.py, quiet and non-quiet chat -q paths).
  Nothing was sent after the stop; the candidate on the tree, verification
  evidence and deadlines are untouched.
- Reaper (detect_crashed_workers): a run with a persisted deferral ends with
  the neutral rate_limited outcome whatever the exit status (also after a
  dispatcher restart lost the reap record): source-phase requeue (ready or
  review), no _record_task_failure, no counter increment or reset; the run
  metadata carries retry_not_before; last_failure_error states the local
  wait and that the previous run's work stays on the tree (worker context).
- Respawn guard: a latest rate_limited run with a local deferral holds the
  card (local_budget_wait) until retry_not_before AND a free slot in the
  shared ledger (peek, no slot taken); the native atomic claim then resumes
  the same card. A newer genuine failure or a manual stop supersedes it.
  Provider 429 handling is unchanged.
